  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2012-p16.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Connect the centers of the three circles. This forms an equilateral triangle of side \\(4\\), with area \\(4\\sqrt3\\).\n\nThe included part of each circle is a \\(300^\\circ\\) sector, whose area is \\(\\dfrac{300}{360}\\pi\\cdot2^2=\\dfrac{10\\pi}{3}\\).\n\nThe total area is \\(3\\cdot\\dfrac{10\\pi}{3}+4\\sqrt3=10\\pi+4\\sqrt3\\).\n\nThus, A is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Connect the three circle centers",
        "The desired area is three \\(300^\\circ\\) sectors plus an equilateral triangle"
      ],
